 "title": "County Treasurer | Ontonagon County",
 "text": "County Treasurer | Ontonagon County\nToggle navigation\nOntonagon County\nHome\nCounty Offices\n911 Director\nAirport\nBoard of Commissioners\nCircuit Court\nCounty Clerk & Register of Deeds\nCounty Park\nCounty Road Commission\nCounty Treasurer\nDistrict Court\nEmergency Services\nEqualization Department\nFriend of the Court\nEconomic Development Corporation\nMedical Examiner\nMine Inspector\nMSU Extension\nOn-Tran\nProbate Court\nProsecutor\nSheriff Department\nSoil Erosion\nTownships\nBergland Township\nBohemia Township\nCarp Lake Township\nGreenland Township\nHaight Township\nInterior Township\nMatchwood Township\nMcMillan Township\nOntonagon Township\nRockland Township\nStannard Township\nCounty Information\nLibraries\nSchool Districts\nVillage of Ontonagon\nElections\nVeterans Service Officer\nCalendar of Events\nCounty Treasurer\nPay 2025 and prior years delinquent property taxes due to Ontonagon County with credit or debit cards! Click below to pay online. You can also contact our office at (906)884-4665 if you would like to make a payment by phone.\nPROPERTY TAX INFORMATION\nView your property tax information through our online portal.\nOntonagon County Public Land Auction\nView available tax auction properties available in Ontonagon County.\nProperty Tax Information Prior to 2000\nAll Ontonagon County and Townships’ property tax roll books dated 1999 and prior have been sent to the archives in Lansing. The public is welcome to go to Lansing and review volumes that are onsite at an offsite storage facility, or they can make a research request at the Michiganology store: https://shop.michiganology.org/products/general-research\nIn the Notes field, list the specific year, township, and the parcel number. There is a charge for the research and the turnaround with research requests is generally 21-28 business days.\nMichigan Public Land Auction | Tax-Sale.info\nHow to Ask For Your Leftover Money After a Tax Foreclosure\nHow to Ask for Your Leftover Money After a Tax Foreclosure | Michigan Legal Help\nOFFICE PHONE: 906-884-4665\nLocated on the First Floor in the Courthouse\nMichele Smith, Treasurer\nmsmith@ontonagoncounty.org\nKaren Morris, Chief Deputy\nkmorris@ontonagoncounty.org\nCopyright © 2016-2017 Ontonagon County. All Rights Reserved.\nSimple Business Theme\nPowered by WordPress",
